hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24052","Narrated to us Mutamir, from his father, from a man, from Ubayd, freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command prayer after the prescribed, or besides the prescribed? He said: Yes, between Maghrib and Isha."
"24053","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Sulayman, and Ibn Abi Adi from Sulayman, the meaning, from a man who narrated to them in the gathering of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi. Ibn Abi Adi said: from an elder in the gathering of Abu Uthman, from Ubayd, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that two women fasted, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, here are two women who have fasted, and they have nearly died of thirst. So he turned away from him, or was silent. Then he returned, and I think he said: in the midday heat. He said: O Prophet of Allah, they, by Allah, have died or nearly died. He said: Call them. He said: So they came. He said: So a cup or large bowl was brought. So he said to one of them: Vomit. So she vomited pus or blood and purulent matter and flesh, until she vomited half the cup. Then he said to the other: Vomit. So she vomited pus and blood and purulent matter and fresh flesh and other, until she filled the cup. Then he said: These two fasted from what Allah allowed, and broke fast upon what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made forbidden to them. One of them sat with the other, and they kept eating the flesh of people."
"24054","Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud, narrated to us Shubah, from al-Taymi, he said: A man came upon us in the gathering of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, and narrated to us from Ubayd, freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was asked about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned his prayer between Maghrib and Isha."
"24055","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated to us Uthman ibn Ghiyath, he said: I was with Abu Uthman. He said: So a man of the people said: Saad or Ubayd narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ghiyath is the one who doubts, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that they were commanded to fast. He said: Then a man came in part of the day and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so and so-and-so have been exhausted. And he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Yazid and Ibn Abi Ubayd from Sulayman."
